# Walking directions against the FAKE cloud (test/EXPECTED.md, "Walking directions", N27). The fake cloud
# scripts the tool calls (`fake tool ...`), the position is the SIMULATED one (walking at 1.2 m/s times
# WALKER_SIM_WALK_SPEEDUP, default 3) and the map services are the responses recorded in
# test/fixtures/navigation/, so the run is offline and repeats. About 5 minutes in real time.
# Run (from devices/pi): node dist/walker.mjs simulate --script test/sim/navigation.walk

# 1. Boot.
expect spoke Sophi is on.
expect link online
expect heartbeat ok

# 2. "Where am I?": the simulated position says it is simulated.
fake tool get_location
key t
expect mic open
wait 1200
key t
expect spoke Fake cloud: Your simulated GPS puts you near 451 Lee Street, Oakland, California.

# 3. "Take me to the Lake Merritt Boating Center": the route starts (the screen's view is on), the fake
# cloud's reply carries the walker's result, then the Pi says its own first line.
fake tool start_route Lake Merritt Boating Center
key t
expect mic open
wait 1200
key t
expect spoke Fake cloud: let me find that.
expect navigation guiding
expect spoke Fake cloud: Walking directions started to Lake Merritt Boating Center: about 750 meters
expect spoke Walking to the Lake Merritt Boating Center, about 750 meters. Head west on the path. Directions come from OpenStreetMap and may include steps or curbs.

# 4. Walking: the Lenox Avenue turn, ahead of it and at it.
expect 30000 spoke turn left onto Lenox Avenue.
expect 30000 spoke Turn left now.

# 5. Confirm with nothing else to confirm says the next instruction again.
key c
expect spoke urn left
absent 1500 cue nothing_to_confirm

# 6. 50 m off the route (to its right, where the route is far): two positions later the walker plans again
# from there and says the new first instruction.
gps off_route 50
expect 10000 spoke You seem to be off the route. Finding the way again.
expect 10000 spoke Head
expect navigation guiding

# 7. On to the end: the arrival, then the route ends 20 s later.
expect 400000 spoke You've arrived near the Lake Merritt Boating Center.
expect navigation arrived
expect 30000 navigation none

# 8. A second route, from the start again, ended by "Stop the directions" (`stop_route`).
gps at 37.8098 -122.2575
fake tool start_route Lake Merritt Boating Center
key t
expect mic open
wait 1200
key t
expect spoke Walking to the Lake Merritt Boating Center
expect navigation guiding
fake tool stop_route
key t
expect mic open
wait 1200
key t
expect spoke Fake cloud: Stopped the directions to the Lake Merritt Boating Center.
expect navigation none
key q
